Write a C program to read Two One Dimensional Arrays of same data type (integer type) and merge them into another One Dimensional Array of same type. Accept an integer and delete that element from the merged array. (3)

Sample I/O:

```text
Enter the number of elements in the first array: 3
Enter 3 elements for the first array:
1       3       4
Enter the number of elements in the second array: 2
Enter 2 elements for the second array:
22      33
Merged array is:
1 3 4 22 33
Enter the element to delete: 22
Final Array after deletion: 1 3 4 33
```

Marking Scheme:
- Variable declaration, reading limit and array elements: ½ M
- Logic for merging: 1M
- Logic for deletion: 1 M (if all the occurrences deleted full marks; only one occurrence then ½ marks)
- Result display: ½ M

```c
#include <stdio.h>
int main() {
int a[10], b[10], merged[20];
int sizeA, sizeB, i, j,n,delKey,found=0;
printf("Enter the number of elements in the first array: ");
scanf("%d", &sizeA);
printf("Enter %d elements for the first array:\n", sizeA);
for(i = 0; i < sizeA; i++)
    scanf("%d", &a[i]);

printf("Enter the number of elements in the second array: ");
scanf("%d", &sizeB);

printf("Enter %d elements for the second array:\n", sizeB);
for(i = 0; i < sizeB; i++)
    scanf("%d", &b[i]);

// Merging arrays
for(i = 0; i < sizeA; i++)
    merged[i] = a[i];
for(j = 0; j < sizeB; j++)
    merged[i + j] = b[j];

// Displaying the merged array
printf("Merged array is:\n");
for(i = 0; i < sizeA + sizeB; i++)
    printf("%d ", merged[i]);
printf("\n");

n=sizeA + sizeB;
printf("Enter the integer to be deleted: ");
scanf("%d", &delKey);
for (i = 0; i < n; i++) {
    if (merged[i] == delKey) {
        found = 1;
        // Shift elements to the left
        for (j = i; j < n - 1; j++) {
            merged[j] = merged[j + 1];
        }
        n--; // Decrement the size of the array
        i--;
    }
}

if (!found) {
    printf("Element %d not found in the array.\n", delKey);
}
printf("Final Array after deletion:\n");
for(i = 0; i < n; i++)
    printf("%d ", merged[i]);

return 0;
}
```

