Given an array of integers (duplicates allowed), write a C program to print all the elements that appear only once (unique elements). (2)

Marking Scheme:
- Initialization od array: 0.5M
- Logic for printing unique elements: 1M
- Display : 0.5M

```c
#include <stdio.h>
int main() {
int arr[10],n ;
int i, j, count;
printf("Enter the array limit: ");
scanf("%d", &n);
printf("Enter the array elements: ");
for(i=0;i<n;i++)
    scanf("%d", &arr[i]);

printf("The array entered: ");
for(i=0;i<n;i++)
    printf("%d ", arr[i]);

printf("\nUnique elemennnts are: ");
for (i = 0; i < n; i++) {
    count = 0;
    for (j = 0; j < n; j++) {
        if (arr[i] == arr[j]) {
            count++;
        }
    }
    if (count == 1) {  // appears only once
        printf("%d ", arr[i]);
    }
}
return 0;
}
```
